# Copy to .env.order-desk next to docker-compose.order-desk.yml, in /srv/agents/order-desk (RUNBOOK-order-desk.md, "The env files"). The copy has mode 600 on the host.
# Names, placeholders and published values only: this example holds no key, no secret and no usable token.
# The service reads this file and no other. Each runtime reads this file first and then the file of its own (.env.order-desk-small, .env.order-desk-medium or .env.order-desk-large, made from .env.order-desk-runtime.example).
# A name that stood in both files would get the value of the second one, so no name stands in both. The four supplier lines of a runtime are only in its own file.
# The copy holds two secrets: the key of the service, and the token between the service and the three runtimes. It never enters git: the .gitignore of the repository covers .env.* except *.example.
# The compose file sets PORT, HOST, ORDER_DESK_STATE_DIR and the settings of each runtime (its service address, its check before the Claim, its timeout, its card origin and its release watcher). Its values win over this file, and the service and the runtimes need different ports.
# So none of these names stands here. The window of the adverts is the one value that both sides read: the compose file gives it to the runtimes, and the service reads it from this file. A test holds the two equal.
# A container reads its env files when it is created. After a change, create the container again: restart does not read them (RUNBOOK-order-desk.md, "The restart rule").
# A value that breaks a rule stops the start of the service, and the error names the variable and never shows the value.
# The key of the service. It pays for the model hire of each decision, signs the claims and the challenges of the dispute code, and signs the request for the X.509-SVID. It is a key of its own: never a supplier key of a runtime.
# The compose file blanks it for the three runtimes. The service derives the key hash from the key. When ORDER_DESK_SERVICE_PKH has a value, it must be that hash, or the service stops at start.
# Both lines are empty here on purpose: the service stops at start without the key. Make the key on the host and write it with a command that prints nothing (RUNBOOK-order-desk.md, "The env files").
ORDER_DESK_SERVICE_PRIV_KEY_HEX=
ORDER_DESK_SERVICE_PKH=
# The token between the service and the three runtimes. Each runtime sends this value, as it stands, as the authorization header of every call to the service. The service answers POST / and POST /precheck only to a call that carries it.
# The form is "Bearer <64 hex characters>", with the quotes: the value has a space. Docker Compose takes the quotes off. The three runtimes and the service read this one line, so they always hold one value.
# Empty here on purpose: the service stops at start without it, so a step that was forgotten cannot leave a service that answers anyone. The value stays in this file. Never paste it into a chat or a log.
SERVICE_AUTH_HEADER=""
# The chain. The runtimes read these lines (the service reads the identity lines below). They hold public values of Vector mainnet: the network, the node, the time of slot 0, and the reference scripts of the escrow and the advert.
# LIVE_CHAIN=1 lets a runtime write to the chain, and the release watcher needs it. ESCROW_REF_UTXO and ADVERT_REF_UTXO are the scripts of the legacy escrow and advert. Keep them while legacy escrows exist.
NETWORK_ID=1
OGMIOS_URL=https://ogmios.vector.mainnet.apexfusion.org
VECTOR_ZERO_TIME_MS=1756485600000
LIVE_CHAIN=1
ESCROW_REF_UTXO=c8d84c6d67ec67a1efe5e9c6c06d53020e05d1bb96d1c55ecb1eb7d5010c4d54#0
ADVERT_REF_UTXO=c8d84c6d67ec67a1efe5e9c6c06d53020e05d1bb96d1c55ecb1eb7d5010c4d54#1
# The identity registry deployment. The lines hold the values that the deployment on Vector mainnet published on 2026-11-03.
# A runtime works an escrow that names the agent with IDENTITY_POLICY_ID, the two scripts below and the AGENT_ID of its own file. IDENTITY_ESCROW_REF_UTXO and IDENTITY_ADVERT_REF_UTXO are the scripts of the escrow and the advert that carry an agent id.
IDENTITY_POLICY_ID=d958b823faaa76977d0a07bd9622e87d8e2c85f6692f7f8e8db77762
IDENTITY_ESCROW_REF_UTXO=4c2d09858dab0cc22cc77dcb99efed570d909a66e0beb512041dea91005b5e82#0
IDENTITY_ADVERT_REF_UTXO=5efd18a1d90a6b87f1fd4b6fe93acfbe5be082260fd52be194b1088ade7c2758#0
# The service reads the four VECTOR_IDENTITY lines for the escrows that it posts. VECTOR_IDENTITY_LEGACY_ROOT is the Merkle root of the adoption allowlist, and VECTOR_IDENTITY_CONFIG_SEED is the output of the seal of the configuration.
# VECTOR_IDENTITY_ESCROW_REF_UTXO and VECTOR_IDENTITY_VAULT_REF_UTXO are the reference scripts of the escrow and of the vault. IDENTITY_POLICY_ID above must be the policy that the root and the output give, or the service stops at start and names the variables.
VECTOR_IDENTITY_LEGACY_ROOT=e4b6b17ce4a8f83aa17d3181ea140d2bd76c0cfa8a7c44ad69543800b4a0df01
VECTOR_IDENTITY_CONFIG_SEED=6c9856c70b1101f1a4e9ceb373188608013416eff48c51f5bb62706a65d41a2a#0
VECTOR_IDENTITY_ESCROW_REF_UTXO=4c2d09858dab0cc22cc77dcb99efed570d909a66e0beb512041dea91005b5e82#0
VECTOR_IDENTITY_VAULT_REF_UTXO=d0bf8f73c915fcbf57ddba714256e520a9a0820bc9e643218db8cf54762d215b#0
# IDENTITY_ADDRESS is the address of the identity registry. Empty means the address of IDENTITY_POLICY_ID, which is right here.
IDENTITY_ADDRESS=
# The Module-1 deployment manifest. The dispute code reads it at start: a challenge needs its scripts and its parameters. It is an https address pinned to one commit of the repository of the Module-1 deployment.
# Replace the placeholder <commit> with the 40 hex digits of the commit that the hosted MCP server uses for its VECTOR_MODULE1_MANIFEST (RUNBOOK-order-desk.md, "The env files"). The manifest at that commit must name the identity registry of IDENTITY_POLICY_ID, or the service stops at start.
VECTOR_MODULE1_MANIFEST=https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Apex-Fusion/vector-agent-modules/<commit>/Module-1/deploy/identity/mainnet/manifest.json
# The services that the checks, the hires and the dispute code read. Each line is empty here, and an empty line keeps the default of the code, which is Vector mainnet. Set a line only to use another service.
# VECTOR_OGMIOS_URL is the node. VECTOR_KOIOS_URL is the indexer of the ledger. VECTOR_SUBMIT_URL takes the transactions. VECTOR_MARKETPLACE_INDEXER_URL is the marketplace indexer. IDENTITY_GATEWAY_URL is the identity gateway.
VECTOR_OGMIOS_URL=
VECTOR_KOIOS_URL=
VECTOR_SUBMIT_URL=
VECTOR_MARKETPLACE_INDEXER_URL=
IDENTITY_GATEWAY_URL=
# The two hosts of the mock systems (deploy/server/README.md, "The two mock host names"). Both are required. Each value is an https origin: https://, one host name, and no path. The two must be two different hosts.
# MOCK_PUBLIC_BASE is the host of tokens. MOCK_MTLS_BASE is the client-certificate host, where the service presents its X.509-SVID. Each value must name the same host as its block in the Caddy file of the mock systems.
MOCK_PUBLIC_BASE=<https origin of the mock host>
MOCK_MTLS_BASE=<https origin of the mock mtls host>
# The origin of the host of the small runtime. The service serves the lots file there, at /lots.json, and its manifest holds the hash of that file.
# The first label of the host name ends in -small. The host names of the medium and the large runtime are the same name with -medium and -large in place of -small, and the service derives them. A name that does not fit stops the start.
LOTS_PUBLIC_ORIGIN=https://mp-suppliers-orders-small.vector.apexfusion.org
# The public values of the three supplier keys, for the service. It publishes them in its manifest. Each public key must hash to the key hash on the line before it, or the service stops at start.
# Write the same values that stand in the SUPPLIER_PKH and SUPPLIER_PUB_KEY_HEX lines of the file of that runtime. The three keys must differ from each other and from the key of the service. Empty here on purpose.
SMALL_SUPPLIER_PKH=
SMALL_SUPPLIER_PUB_KEY_HEX=
MEDIUM_SUPPLIER_PKH=
MEDIUM_SUPPLIER_PUB_KEY_HEX=
LARGE_SUPPLIER_PKH=
LARGE_SUPPLIER_PUB_KEY_HEX=
# The window of the three adverts, in milliseconds: 8 minutes. The manifest publishes it. The compose file gives the runtimes the same value, and the service does not start with less than 480000.
ADVERT_MAX_PROCESSING_MS=480000
# The manifest. What the service serves at /agent.json is hashed into the three adverts, so each line below must be final before the hash is taken. A change afterwards means retired adverts and new ones.
# OPERATOR_CONTACT is required and is published. It is the contact address that the live agents of the operator publish. The operator types it, and no file of the repository holds it. AGENT_DID is written when the agent record exists: did:vector: and the 64 hex characters of AGENT_ID.
# AGENT_VERSION stays empty: the service has its own default. AGENT_STATUS_CHIP is proposed, deployed or live. Empty AGENT_STATUS_SINCE keeps the date of the build, and a date as YYYY-MM-DD goes with a change of the word.
# ADVERT_EXPLORER_URL stays empty: the transaction of an advert cannot be inside the manifest that the advert hashes.
OPERATOR_CONTACT=<contact address that the live agents publish>
AGENT_DID=
AGENT_VERSION=
AGENT_STATUS_CHIP=proposed
AGENT_STATUS_SINCE=
ADVERT_EXPLORER_URL=
# The check before the Claim. A runtime asks the service, and waits 10 seconds for the answer. The service makes six timed reads one after the other, and each read ends inside this budget in milliseconds.
# Empty keeps 1200. The budget times 6 must be under 9000, so 1499 is the most. Leave it empty unless a read of the ledger or the gateway is too slow.
CHECKS_READ_BUDGET_MS=
# What the service hires for its decision, whether the lot can be supplied. The line of the allowlist is the model that Advocate hires too: the models, comma separated with no space, in order of preference.
# LLM_MAX_PRICE_LOVELACE is the most that a model hire may be priced at: 1000000 lovelace, 1 unit. The two bond lines limit the supplier bond and the buyer bond of the model advert. Every such advert has bonds of 1000000, so 2000000 is the limit for each.
# All four lines are required, and the service never fills one in for you.
LLM_MODEL_ALLOWLIST=deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash
LLM_MAX_PRICE_LOVELACE=1000000
LLM_MAX_SUPPLIER_BOND_LOVELACE=2000000
LLM_MAX_BUYER_BOND_LOVELACE=2000000
# The dispute code. The stake of a challenge, in lovelace: the Module-1 deployment on Vector mainnet asks at least 50000000 for a claim, and a challenge targets a claim whose stake is not above this value. So this is the least stake.
# DISPUTE_MIN_WINDOW_LEFT_MS is the least time that a claim must still have in its challenge window: 600000, 10 minutes. DISPUTE_READ_TIMEOUT_MS is the most time that one read of the dispute code may take.
# The last two lines are optional and empty. The service takes the resolution deadline from the Module-1 deployment, and a value here must be equal to it or the start stops. A lease is how long an unfinished challenge blocks a second try for its escrow.
DISPUTE_CHALLENGE_STAKE_LOVELACE=50000000
DISPUTE_MIN_WINDOW_LEFT_MS=600000
DISPUTE_READ_TIMEOUT_MS=20000
DISPUTE_RESOLUTION_DEADLINE_MS=
DISPUTE_STARTED_LEASE_MS=
# The fault switch of the service. It is empty in a clean run. The one other value is confirm_wrong_lot, for a failure run: the confirmation then names another lot than the purchase order.
# Any other value stops the start. The manifest does not change with the switch, so the adverts stay valid. Set it only as RUNBOOK-order-desk.md says ("The fault switch"): never during a run.
FAULT_MODE=
